  "question": "求级数 $\\sum_{n=3}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(n-2)n2^n}$ 的和.",
  "answer": "$$ \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\frac {1}{(n - 2) n 2 ^ {n}} = S \\left(\\frac {1}{2}\\right) = \\frac {5}{1 6} - \\frac {3}{8} \\ln 2. $$",
  "ref_source": "textbook:puheping_math_contest_v2",
  "techniques": [
    "积分技巧",
    "收敛半径与收敛域"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "text": "分析 比较常见的方法是构造适当的幂级数，将所求级数的值作为幂级数和函数的值来计算。构造幂级数的方式可能不止一种，要以和函数容易计算为宜。"
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "text": "$$\n\\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\frac {1}{(n - 2) n 2 ^ {n}} = \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\left(\\frac {1}{n - 2} - \\frac {1}{n}\\right) \\frac {1}{2 ^ {n + 1}} = \\frac {1}{2 ^ {3}} \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\frac {1}{n - 2} \\cdot \\frac {1}{2 ^ {n - 2}} - \\frac {1}{2} \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\frac {1}{n} \\cdot \\frac {1}{2 ^ {n}}.\n$$"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "text": "令 $S(x) = \\frac{1}{2^3}\\sum_{n = 3}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n - 2} x^{n - 2} - \\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{n = 3}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{n} x^n$ ，则"
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "text": "$$\nS ^ {\\prime} (x) = \\frac {1}{2 ^ {3}} \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} x ^ {n - 3} - \\frac {1}{2} \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} x ^ {n - 1} = \\frac {1}{2 ^ {3}} \\cdot \\frac {1}{1 - x} - \\frac {1}{2} \\cdot \\frac {x ^ {2}}{1 - x} = \\frac {3}{2 ^ {3}} \\cdot \\frac {1}{1 - x} + \\frac {1}{2} (1 + x), | x | <   1.\n$$"
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "text": "积分，并注意 $S(0) = 0$ 得"
      },
      {
        "id": "s6",
        "text": "$$\nS (x) = \\frac {3}{2 ^ {3}} \\int_ {0} ^ {x} \\frac {\\mathrm{d} t}{1 - t} + \\frac {1}{2} \\int_ {0} ^ {x} (1 + t) \\mathrm{d} t = - \\frac {3}{2 ^ {3}} \\ln (1 - x) + \\frac {1}{2} \\left(x + \\frac {1}{2} x ^ {2}\\right).\n$$"
      },
      {
        "id": "s7",
        "text": "所以"
      },
      {
        "id": "s8",
        "text": "$$\n\\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\frac {1}{(n - 2) n 2 ^ {n}} = S \\left(\\frac {1}{2}\\right) = \\frac {5}{1 6} - \\frac {3}{8} \\ln 2.\n$$"
      }
    ],
    "final_answer": "$$ \\sum_ {n = 3} ^ {\\infty} \\frac {1}{(n - 2) n 2 ^ {n}} = S \\left(\\frac {1}{2}\\right) = \\frac {5}{1 6} - \\frac {3}{8} \\ln 2. $$",
